//共にある。
  <I>Cursed...</I> Yes, I remember now. If you look back through the annals of history, no tsurugi is more closely associated with that word than those which bore the name Muramasa.

//　大和史上ほかに例のない程に、長く果てしなく意義
//もなく続いた泥沼の大乱――南北朝争乱。
//　嘘か真か、その地獄を演出したのはある鍛冶一門の
//鍛え上げた劒冑だと云う。
  They appeared, it is said, during the Nanbokucho War, one of the bloodiest conflicts in Yamatoan history, and are credited with dragging that war into the pointless, inescapable mire that made it so.

//　妖甲、勢洲右衛門尉村正。
//　……この赤い蜘蛛こそが、それであるならば。
  If this crimson spider is truly one of that line, one of the tsurugi that turned Yamato into hell on earth, then―

